+    *   *For Particle-Based Models (e.g., DAP-NeRF):* Compute the velocity directly from particle motions by averaging the velocities of particles affecting the voxel region at time $t$ [S1]. Particle velocity is $v_p = \frac{p_{t+\delta t} - p_t}{\delta t}$ [S1].
+4.  **Calculate Error:** Compute the Euclidean norm difference $\|F_1(x_n) - F_2(x_n)\|_2$ for each voxel [S1].
 5.  **Aggregate:** Average the errors over all $N$ voxels to obtain the MFE [S1].
 
